{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007;\n\nstruct DSU {\n    vector<i64> parent;\n    vector<i64> rank;\n\n    DSU(i64 n) : parent(n), rank(n, 0) {\n        for (i64 i = 0; i < n; ++i) parent[i] = i;\n    }\n\n    i64 find(i64 x) {\n        if (parent[x] != x) parent[x] = find(parent[x]);\n        return parent[x];\n    }\n\n    void unite(i64 x, i64 y) {\n        x = find(x); y = find(y);\n        if (x == y) return;\n        if (rank[x] < rank[y]) swap(x, y);\n        parent[y] = x;\n        if (rank[x] == rank[y]) ++rank[x];\n    }\n};\n\ni64 count_cycles(i64 p, i64 k) {\n    DSU dsu(p);\n    for (i64 i = 1; i < p; ++i) {\n        i64 ki = (k * i) % p;\n        dsu.unite(i, ki);\n    }\n    vector<bool> seen(p, false);\n    i64 cnt = 0;\n    for (i64 i = 1; i < p; ++i) {\n        i64 r = dsu.find(i);\n        if (!seen[r]) {\n            seen[r] = true;\n            ++cnt;\n        }\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\n\ni64 count_solutions(i64 p, i64 k) {\n    i64 cycles;\n    if (k == 0) cycles = p - 1;\n    else if (k == 1) cycles = p;\n    else cycles = count_cycles(p, k);\n\n    i64 res = 1;\n    for (i64 i = 0; i < cycles; ++i) {\n        res = (res * p) % MOD;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    i64 p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    cout << count_solutions(p, k) << '\\n';\n    int dummy;\n    cin >> dummy;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\nclass DSU:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.parent = list(range(n))\n        self.rank = [0] * n\n    \n    def find(self, x):\n        if self.parent[x] != x:\n            self.parent[x] = self.find(self.parent[x])\n        return self.parent[x]\n    \n    def unite(self, x, y):\n        x = self.find(x)\n        y = self.find(y)\n        if x == y:\n            return\n        if self.rank[x] < self.rank[y]:\n            x, y = y, x\n        self.parent[y] = x\n        if self.rank[x] == self.rank[y]:\n            self.rank[x] += 1\n\ndef count_cycles(p, k):\n    dsu = DSU(p)\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        ki = (k * i) % p\n        dsu.unite(i, ki)\n    seen = [False] * p\n    cnt = 0\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        r = dsu.find(i)\n        if not seen[r]:\n            seen[r] = True\n            cnt += 1\n    return cnt\n\ndef count_solutions(p, k):\n    if k == 0:\n        cycles = p - 1\n    elif k == 1:\n        cycles = p\n    else:\n        cycles = count_cycles(p, k)\n    \n    res = 1\n    for i in range(cycles):\n        res = (res * p) % MOD\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    p = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    print(count_solutions(p, k))\n    # Read the dummy value to match the original behavior\n    if len(data) > 2:\n        dummy = int(data[2])\n    else:\n        dummy = int(input())\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012766500003635883, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.40889808535575867, -0.0001245659514097497, -6.794698856538162e-05, -0.02394123002886772, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0028117666952311993, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00010930894495686516, -2.5033637939486653e-05, -1.1444026313256472e-05, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.13667045533657074, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -7.510157047363464e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -3.099436753473128e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -2.50339189733495e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.4781842764932662e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -4.291525328881107e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0004717191040981561, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.076874756719917e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.38418